{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>For I was afraid of the anger</b>. He says: because of the anger and the wrath with which HaShem was enraged against you from the outset to destroy you, I was afraid even now — for there still remains upon you [the threat] of destruction because of that great fury, even though HaShem had already relented concerning the evil that He had spoken of doing to His people. Therefore I turned again and fell prostrate for your sake forty days and forty nights, until He heard me also on that occasion just as He heard on the first occasion before I came down. And I also prayed on behalf of Aaron on this occasion when I returned there, for until he burned up the calf he attended only to turning back His wrath from destroying the people at that moment."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T02:47:13.358896124Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}